{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1404395-demon-blooded-has-twin-help-needed","id":1404395,"title":"Demon-Blooded has twin, help needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-24T07:17:32-07:00","id":1404395,"title":"Demon-Blooded has twin, help needed","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> So, the premise for one of the PCs in my campaign is that she's a twin. Her twin brother and she were captives of a Stigmatics Conversion Therapy camp in Japan before they were rescued. The two of them were being trained by an Angel to use their Biokinesis to be the perfect infiltration killers for the God-Machine. If you're one of my players reading this, you know this much and now is your chance to look away.<br /> <br /> <br /> The twin sister is the PC, the twin brother is the NPC. The player has established that the brother is the more cold, analytical one, and stayed loyal to their Angelic handler even though he's disappeared. He's been told that &quot;One must kill the Other.&quot;<br /> The two of them can shape shift to look like anyone else (Hurt Locker rules for Doppelganger).<br /> <br /> Using that, and an analytical mind, how would you go about trying to kill the sister?<br /> <br /> So far, I've had him show up disguised as the sister to one of the other PC's that the sister is romantically involved with to scout them out. I'm looking for something potentially sinister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25927-lolotovcocktail","name":"LolotovCocktail","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:46:08-07:00","id":1404517,"title":"","content":"Some questions for you:<br /> <br /> 1. Is there a particular way Brother wants Sister to die? Luring her to an abandoned warehouse and shooting her is the most straightforward thing to do, but it doesn't raise a lot of options for an eleventh-hour rescue by the rest of the PCs or a dramatic villain monologue from Brother. Does he want to torture her for her sins against the G-M? That means he has to set up a place for the torture to happen. Does he want her death to look accidental, or to frame one of the other PCs for it? That requires different arrangements.<br /> <br /> 2. How many chances do you want to give the PCs to catch on to his scheme? The more interactions he has with them, even if he's in disguise, the more opportunities they have to recognize something's amiss, even if they don't jump directly to the right answer. On the other hand, you can heighten the ring's paranoia without giving them opportunities to identify Brother. They see a shadowy figure watching them, but he escapes before they can give chase; a Demon PC's cover might start to degrade but they don't know who's behind it; etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T18:56:26-07:00","id":1404687,"title":"","content":"Honestly one way that he could do this would be to take on her appearances and commit crimes in order to apply pressure as police try to apprehend her. Then if he can he could take the guise of either a police officer or one who can shelter her. Either way, construct a scenario where she is chased or hrrded to her demise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T17:47:42-07:00","id":1404850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1404395-demon-blooded-has-twin-help-needed?p=1404517#post1404517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions for you:<br /> <br /> 1. Is there a particular way Brother wants Sister to die? Luring her to an abandoned warehouse and shooting her is the most straightforward thing to do, but it doesn't raise a lot of options for an eleventh-hour rescue by the rest of the PCs or a dramatic villain monologue from Brother. Does he want to torture her for her sins against the G-M? That means he has to set up a place for the torture to happen. Does he want her death to look accidental, or to frame one of the other PCs for it? That requires different arrangements.<br /> <br /> 2. How many chances do you want to give the PCs to catch on to his scheme? The more interactions he has with them, even if he's in disguise, the more opportunities they have to recognize something's amiss, even if they don't jump directly to the right answer. On the other hand, you can heighten the ring's paranoia without giving them opportunities to identify Brother. They see a shadowy figure watching them, but he escapes before they can give chase; a Demon PC's cover might start to degrade but they don't know who's behind it; etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>3. How much preparation does the Brother need to do (such as research) before they can properly mimic someone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T17:49:41-07:00","id":1405705,"title":"","content":"Also imitate her allies and cast doubt on whether she can trust them. They could be &quot;seen&quot; with obvious GM allies. Make it so that she will never know if the person from whom she is seeking help is really who she thinks it is. <br /> <br /> DtD is at its best in an espionage game. Make plans within plans, and make it so she can't be sure of her allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}